  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a data management system to track officer-involved shootings as reported by the Dallas Police Department. This system aims to provide structured and accessible data concerning incidents, involved officers, and subjects or suspects.\n\n2) Objectives\n\n- To systematically record and manage data related to officer-involved shootings.\n- To offer comprehensive details about each incident, including the parties involved, demographic details, locations, and outcomes.\n- To support transparency and accessibility of information regarding the incidents through web-based summaries and documents.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Stakeholders: Dallas Police Department, legal entities, community organizations, policy makers.\n- Users: Department data analysts, law enforcement officers, researchers, journalists, and the general public.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Incident Management: The system will store and manage detailed records of each shooting incident, including the date, location, subject status, and weapon information.\n- Officer Management: Capture and manage demographic information of officers involved in incidents.\n- Subject Management: Capture and manage demographic details of subjects involved in incidents.\n- Data Linking: Each officer and subject is linked to their respective incidents to maintain cohesive data integrity.\n- Report Generation: Provide options to generate reports containing incident summaries and available external document links.\n- External Access: Facilitate public and stakeholders' access to non-confidential summaries and related documents.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Security: Ensure data confidentiality, especially the sensitive demographic information of officers and subjects.\n- Scalability: Support an expanding database as new incidents are recorded over time.\n- Performance: Efficiently manage queries and data updates to ensure quick information retrieval.\n- Usability: Design a user-friendly interface that is accessible and easy to navigate by all types of users.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0104\nCREATE TABLE `incidents` (\n  `incident_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `incident_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `incident_time` time DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `state` char(2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `subject_status` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `weapon_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `summary` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `external_document_url` varchar(500) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`incident_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `officers` (\n  `officer_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `incident_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `badge_number` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `race_ethnicity` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `rank_title` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role_in_incident` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`officer_id`),\n  KEY `officers_ibfk_1` (`incident_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `officers_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`incident_id`) REFERENCES `incidents` (`incident_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `subjects` (\n  `subject_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `incident_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `race_ethnicity` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `armed_status` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `injury_status` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `outcome` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`subject_id`),\n  KEY `subjects_ibfk_1` (`incident_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `subjects_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`incident_id`) REFERENCES `incidents` (`incident_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
